{
  "kanji": "冒",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 冒\ntitle: brave danger; venture\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 冂\nradicalNumber: 13\nonyomi: [ボウ]\nkunyomi: [おか.す]\nquizOnyomi: [ボウ]\nquizKunyomi: [おか.す]\ndistractors: [日, 目, 官]\n---\n\n# 冒 — brave danger; venture\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 冂 (the outer outline of the upper part, no. 13) · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n冒 expresses braving danger or venturing despite difficulty in [冒す](../words/冒す.md) (おかす) and [冒険](../words/冒険.md) (ぼうけん), \"adventure; risky venture.\"\nIt is not a general label for anything dangerous: [危険](../words/危険.md) (きけん) names danger, while 危険を冒す (きけんをおかす) means taking a risk.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture an eye, [目](目.md), beneath a boxlike upper outline, looking ahead despite danger.\nThis is a memory aid, not a historical sun-plus-eye explanation. The classical indexing radical is 冂, not [日](日.md), even though the upper shape can resemble 日.\n\n## Readings\n\nBoth complete source readings are retained and selected for reading practice.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ボウ | on | [冒険](../words/冒険.md) ぼうけん — adventure; risky venture |\n| おか.す | kun | [冒す](../words/冒す.md) おかす — brave danger; 危険を冒す きけんをおかす — take a risk |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [冒険](../words/冒険.md) ぼうけん — adventure; risky venture\n- [冒す](../words/冒す.md) おかす — brave danger; venture despite difficulty\n- 冒頭 (ぼうとう) — beginning; opening\n\n## Notes\n\nDo not force the risk-taking gloss into every compound: 冒頭 names an opening, not an adventure.\n冒す also has a harm/affliction sense: 病に冒される (やまいにおかされる), \"be afflicted by a disease,\" is passive, not someone choosing to take a risk.\n\n[犯](犯.md) also has the reading おか.す, but 犯す is used for committing an offense, as in 罪を犯す (つみをおかす), \"commit a crime.\"\n侵す (おかす) concerns invading or infringing and can overlap with 冒す in harm/affliction uses. These are useful spelling distinctions, not perfectly separate meaning compartments.\nFor shape comparison, [官](官.md) has a roof and a different connected lower outline; neither 官 nor 目 means braving danger.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1519820, 1519830, 1519860, 1855070, 1868850, 1359800 and 1481550.\nReading and meaning branches: [Digital Daijisen: 冒](https://www.weblio.jp/content/冒); spelling overlap: [Digital Daijisen: 冒す](https://www.weblio.jp/content/冒す).\n",
